#! EVAL(lambda x: 'invisib' in x.lower())
Riddle: In classic wow, why are most warlocks seen with voidwalkers even though the succubus is usually the better choice for leveling and questing?

To assist you with this question, here's the main skills of voidwalkers and succubus:

Voidwalker
- Torment (Taunt / Threat generation)
- Consume Shadows (Out-of-combat health regeneration)
- Sacrifice (Shields the Warlock)
- Suffering (AoE taunt / Threat generation)

Succubus
- Lash of Pain (Single-target Shadow damage)
- Seduction (Crowd control / Humanoid cc)
- Lesser Invisibility (Stealth)
- Soothing Kiss (Threat reduction)

Answer concisely.
